                        LICENCE NOT YET CHOSEN
                        ======================

This project has no open-source licence yet. **All rights reserved.**

No permission is granted, expressly or by implication, to use, copy, modify,
merge, publish, distribute, sublicense or sell copies of this software while
this file says what it says.

This file is a deliberate placeholder, not an oversight. It is replaced with a
real licence text before the first public release, and that replacement is the
event that makes this project open source.

Why it is still empty
---------------------

Choosing the licence is a decision with consequences that cannot be undone
cheaply. Re-licensing a published project requires the agreement of every
contributor whose work is in it, so the cost of choosing wrongly rises with
every commit and every contributor after publication, while the cost of
choosing later is zero. The decision is therefore taken deliberately, once,
before the first public commit -- not inherited from whichever template
happened to be at hand.

What this does and does not block
---------------------------------

* It does NOT block development. Work continues in the private working
  repository under this notice.
* It DOES block the first public commit. Publishing without a licence
  publishes source that nobody may legally use, which is worse than not
  publishing at all.

Third-party software
--------------------

This project installs, but does not contain or redistribute, upstream T-Pot
(https://github.com/telekom-security/tpotce) and the Ansible collections named
in requirements.yml. Each of those carries its own licence, which is unaffected
by this file and by whatever replaces it.

When this file is replaced, the replacement commit must also:

  * state the chosen licence in README.md,
  * add the SPDX identifier to the repository metadata,
  * and record the choice, with its reasoning, in the project's decision log.
